        "abstract": "PALplus has been developed to provide widescreen 16:9 television via a PAL terrestrial channel whilst continuing to serve the existing audience of viewers with 4:3 format TV sets. The equipment was first demonstrated in London in May 1993. This paper looks at the implementation of the PALplus specification on this prototype hardware.<<ETX xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">&gt;</ETX>",
